From: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: context/VM hardening — stop the shared-VM fallback for VM_BIND

msm_gpu_create_private_vm() silently handed back the global kernel-managed VM
when per-process pgtable creation failed, even for a userspace-managed
(EN_VM_BIND) client. Turnip then does its own address management against a VM
it does not own, and the GPU takes a storm of `type=TRANSLATION source=UCHE`
faults -- mesa#14656, reported on A740, which is every qcs8550-* board we ship.
With the series the ioctl fails honestly, tu_try_enable_vm_bind() returns
non-zero and Turnip drops to the legacy submit path instead.

BACKPORT of 12 mainline commits from Rob Clark's 2026-07-29 drm/msm
context/VM hardening series (Message-ID 20260729155609.20190-*, patches
2..18), merged for 7.3, squashed into one diff. None of it is in 7.2.x.
In the order they apply here:

   2/18 ae88499d71ce drm/msm: Fix barriers accessing ctx vm
   3/18 ea69d489d3a6 drm/msm: Rework queuelock
   4/18 2c26f9e46d39 drm/msm: Synchronize VM creation on ctxlock
   9/18 517ca9a86a4a drm/msm: Add helper to check for per-process pgtables VM
  15/18 00dfa76bdfc2 drm/msm: Allow lazy VM creation to fail
  16/18 3b35a5c528ba drm/msm: Don't fallback to shared VM for VM_BIND
  17/18 1b8029394fb7 drm/msm: Fix per-process-pgtables check
  10/18 e6863b085606 drm/msm/gem: Fix dma_buf import error paths
  11/18 4e67b8fc55c4 drm/msm/gem: Remove useless locking in GEM import
  12/18 695d2b042af0 drm/msm/gem: Extract bookkeeping init helper
  13/18 df68029e639b drm/msm/gem: Set resv before exposing obj
  14/18 a6d87a272b2c drm/msm/gem: Validate lazy VM in GEM_NEW

Why each is here:
- 16/18 is the fix we are after; the rest make it safe.
- 2/18 loads/stores ctx->vm with acquire/release instead of relying on
  store ordering; 3/18 turns queuelock into the ctxlock rw_semaphore that
  4/18 reuses to serialise MSM_PARAM_EN_VM_BIND against lazy VM creation
  (two clients racing at startup, a game and steamwebhelper say).
- 9/18 factors out valid_per_process_vm(), which 15/18 teaches to tolerate
  a NULL vm. 15/18 is what makes 16/18 safe: once msm_context_vm() may
  return NULL every caller must check, or a fault storm becomes a NULL
  deref in the submitqueue path. 17/18 fixes the EN_VM_BIND capability
  check that the removed fallback left dead.
- 14/18 closes the one caller 15/18 misses: a _NO_SHARE GEM_NEW read
  ctx->vm directly, NULL before the context has a VM. 10-13/18 are its
  prerequisites, taken verbatim rather than adapting it to the 7.2 shape of
  msm_gem_new(); 13/18 is also a fix in its own right (the resv was swapped
  after the object was already visible on the LRU and object lists).

Not carried: 5/18 (set_sysprof on ctxlock), 6-8/18 and 18/18 — none touch
this path.

Each commit was cherry-picked onto v7.2.7 + this stack with no conflict and
matched its mainline +/- lines exactly. Upstream order is not kept (10-14
come last); the order above is the one that was tested. Drops at 7.3.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index a2f6918c4f7f..f106e94ecc0a 100644
